# ── machine-local, not part of the site ──────────────────────────────────
# There is no package.json here and there must never be one (see CLAUDE.md),
# so a lockfile can only be the residue of a stray `npm install` or of running
# tools/make-icons.mjs. Ignored rather than committed, because committing it
# would be the first half of exactly the version carrier this repo refuses to
# grow.
package-lock.json
node_modules/

# Deploy-time viewer config. Neither value is a secret, but neither belongs in
# git: filling them in would tie this public repo to one project and make
# rotating a key a code change. A deploy writes it.
read/config.js
